Rogue level is not generated in every game (similar as big level). In all
games where I have seen it, it was located between levels 10-15.

How to distinguish a rogue level - it has an unusual (for nethack) map -
there are 9 or less rooms in 3x3 grid (sometimes there are only  corridors
where a room should be), the rooms are therefore usually rather narrow and
long (2xsomething, 3xsomething...), there are no doors. Also on my ATARI,
where I have a fancy font loaded to display walls, corridors etc, the rogue
level is always displayed in ASCII - so it can be recognised immediately.
Apart from that - it is a normal level (I've never seen it contain any
special rooms - Zoos, shops, etc - is it a rule?). Ah, of course, there
is a ghost ;-)
